// A touch-ally cleanse-and-ward. D&D's instant "neutralize an existing
// poison" half has no target-side remove-buff primitive reachable from a
// touch-range `BasicAura` (`AbilityInitEvent::RemoveBuff` fires for the
// caster on ability activation, not for whoever the aura lands on), so that
// half is dropped -- this ships as the preventive-ward half only: a flat
// `ProtectingWard` damage-reduction ward standing in for "resists damage
// from venoms while the warding lasts". `duration: Instant` at the
// compendium level describes the one-action cast, not the ward itself --
// the real 1-hour ward lifespan (matching D&D's own timed duration, per the
// sheet's own note) lives in this file's `auras[].duration`/`aura_duration`,
// the same split snare.ron already uses for its own Instant-cast,
// timed-effect shape.
BasicAura(
    buildup_duration: 0.4,
    cast_duration: 0.2,
    recover_duration: 0.3,
    targets: InGroup,
    auras: [
        (
            kind: ProtectingWard,
            strength: 0.15,
            duration: Some(3600.0),
            category: Some(Magical),
        ),
    ],
    aura_duration: Some(3600.0),
    range: 2.0,
    energy_cost: 25.0,
    scales_with_combo: false,
    specifier: None,
    meta: (school: Some(Abjuration), source: Some(Divine)),
)
